# Now let's do my story

Here's how I approached each of the six steps.

<Screenshot url="reuters.com" href="https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/how-europes-intensifying-marine-heatwaves-threaten-its-fisheries-2026-09-26/" label="Sea-temperature story demo">
  <video
    src="{base}/screenshots/social-science-in-a-hurry/sea-temp-demo.mp4"
    data-autoplay
    loop
    muted
    playsinline
  ></video>
</Screenshot>

</Slide>

<Slide>

<p class="slide-eyebrow">Step 1 of 6</p>

<div class="icon-heading">
  <Lightbulb aria-hidden="true" size={48} strokeWidth={1.75} />
  <h1>Identify measurable questions</h1>
</div>

This story got kicked off by an email from an editor.

<div class="email-card not-prose">
  <div class="email-header">
    <p class="email-field"><span class="email-label">From:</span> <span class="email-value"><span class="redacted">Rachel Armstrong</span></span></p>
    <p class="email-field"><span class="email-label">To:</span> <span class="email-value">Ben, <span class="redacted">Kate</span></span></p>
    <p class="email-field email-field-subject"><span class="email-label">Subject:</span> <span class="email-value">Marine heatwave in Europe</span></p>
    <p class="email-field"><span class="email-label">Date:</span> <span class="email-value">July 23, 2026</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="email-body">
    <p>Hi <span class="redacted">Kate</span>, Ben,</p>
    <p>This is (obviously) not my area of expertise, but from looking at the
    climate monitor during the European heatwave I was noticing how the
    sea, particularly the Med and the Bay of Biscay, seemed to be fairly
    consistently around 10 degrees above the historic average temperature,
    and staying at that level much longer than a lot of land temperatures
    in the region, which have fluctuated above the average a bit more.</p>
    <p>I was wondering, first of all, Ben, if there's a way of extracting
    historical data from the climate monitor to see if that anecdotal
    finding above is correct or not?</p>
    <p>And separately, <span class="redacted">Kate</span>, have you seen much compelling data on sea
    temperatures in Europe this year — I can see some links below from
    Copernicus and a couple of things on the UK, but not sure if there's
    anything more current or broader?</p>
    <p>I was thinking if it's the case that sea temperatures in this region
    have generally been tracking higher above the average historical
    temperature than land ones, then maybe there's scope for a story
    looking at that, and the implications it brings, marrying it with some
    on-the-ground/water reporting?</p>
    <p><span class="redacted">Rachel</span></p>
  </div>
</div>

</Slide>

<Slide>

<p class="slide-eyebrow">Step 2 of 6</p>

<div class="icon-heading">
  <Database aria-hidden="true" size={48} strokeWidth={1.75} />
  <h1>Locate data that can provide the answers</h1>
</div>

I found a dataset with daily sea surface temperatures covering the entire
globe. I interviewed experts to verify it was reliable.

<Screenshot url="ncei.noaa.gov" href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/optimum-interpolation-sst" label="NOAA OISST dataset product page">
  <img
    src="{base}/screenshots/social-science-in-a-hurry/oisst-dataset.png"
    alt="NOAA NCEI product page for the Optimum Interpolation Sea Surface Temperature (OISST) dataset"
  />
</Screenshot>

</Slide>

<Slide>

<p class="slide-eyebrow">Step 3 of 6</p>

<div class="icon-heading">
  <Hammer aria-hidden="true" size={48} strokeWidth={1.75} />
  <h1>Prepare raw data for rigorous analysis</h1>
</div>

One challenge I faced was defining what counts as European waters. After
talking to experts, I went with the regions defined by this government
agency.

<Screenshot url="eea.europa.eu" href="https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/analysis/maps-and-charts/marine-regions-and-subregions" label="European Environment Agency: Marine regions and subregions">
  <img
    src="{base}/screenshots/social-science-in-a-hurry/eea-marine-regions.png"
    alt="European Environment Agency map titled 'Marine regions and subregions,' showing the official boundaries of EU marine regions"
  />
</Screenshot>

</Slide>

<Slide>

<p class="slide-eyebrow">Step 4 of 6</p>

<div class="icon-heading">
  <BarChart3 aria-hidden="true" size={48} strokeWidth={1.75} />
  <h1>Interview prepared data to develop findings</h1>
</div>

I used Python and an AI coding assistant to develop a reproducible notebook
that asked and answered our key questions.

<Screenshot url="github.com" href="https://github.com/palewire/european-marine-heatwave-analysis/blob/main/analysis.ipynb" label="Jupyter notebook: European marine heatwave analysis">
  <img
    src="{base}/screenshots/social-science-in-a-hurry/sea-temp-analysis-notebook.png"
    alt="GitHub-rendered Jupyter notebook showing Python code that averages summer sea-surface temperatures by region and year, with a results table ranking 2026 as the hottest summer on record"
  />
</Screenshot>

</Slide>

<Slide>

<p class="slide-eyebrow">Step 5 of 6</p>

<div class="icon-heading">
  <Map aria-hidden="true" size={48} strokeWidth={1.75} />
  <h1>Test your findings against the real world</h1>
</div>

We traveled to the areas with the most extreme temperatures, interviewing
scientists who study the sea and fishermen who confront the changes every
day.

<img
  src="{base}/screenshots/social-science-in-a-hurry/sea-temp-fisherman.jpg"
  alt="A fisherman points out at the coastline and sea along northern Spain"
  class="cover-image"
/>

</Slide>

<Slide>

<p class="slide-eyebrow">Step 6 of 6</p>

<div class="icon-heading">
  <MessageCircle aria-hidden="true" size={48} strokeWidth={1.75} />
  <h1>Ensure subjects have a say in the story</h1>
</div>

While there was no bad actor to confront, anchoring our findings in the
real world showed what's at stake and made this story more than a
statistical exercise.

<Screenshot url="reuters.com" href="https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/how-europes-intensifying-marine-heatwaves-threaten-its-fisheries-2026-09-26/" label="Published story: How Europe's intensifying marine heatwaves threaten its fisheries">
  <img
    src="{base}/screenshots/social-science-in-a-hurry/sea-temp-story-published.png"
    alt="The published Reuters story, showing a fisherman speaking on camera at a harbor about the impact of warming waters on local landings"
  />
</Screenshot>

</Slide>

